<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!-- Grafts the song component onto the anima tree.

       WHY A PATCH AND NOT A DEF OF OUR OWN. `Plant_TreeAnima` belongs to Royalty: the only way to
       give it a component is to patch its def.

       WHY A PLANT CAN CARRY A COMPONENT. `Plant` derives from `ThingWithComps` - the vanilla def
       already declares `CompProperties_MeditationFocus`, `CompProperties_Glower` and
       `CompProperties_SpawnSubplant`. The `<comps>` node therefore always exists, and we add to
       it rather than creating a second one, which would be ignored.

       THIS COMPONENT IS WHAT PROVIDES THE GIZMO. A `ThingWithComps` gets its gizmos from
       `CompGetGizmosExtra`: without this patch the tree stays mute when selected, and nothing
       tells the player the mod is there.

       GUARDED ON THE DEF EXISTING, not on a mod identifier: that is the repository's rule, and
       here it lands right, since without Royalty there is no anima tree at all. An xpath that
       matches nothing would make the loader shout in red. -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Plant_TreeAnima"]/comps</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Plant_TreeAnima"]/comps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="AnimaSong.CompProperties_AnimaSong" />
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
